Shall we Cliff? May I call you Cliff?

01:18:14.910 --> 01:18:16.010
Barney, too much pressure.

01:18:25.920 --> 01:18:26.720
One, two...

01:18:30.670 --> 01:18:32.730
Nice going. Now what do we do?

01:18:32.850 --> 01:18:34.470
You get the kids. I'll try and stop this.

01:19:11.290 --> 01:19:13.690
P.F., I ever told you you have a very distinguished chin.

01:19:14.340 --> 01:19:15.000
Shut up!

01:19:31.680 --> 01:19:34.230
Oh dear, are there too many years behind the desk?

01:19:34.850 --> 01:19:36.050
Mayday! Mayday!

01:19:43.000 --> 01:19:47.780
I'll be done now!

01:19:49.970 --> 01:19:51.670
Oh, flunkhead!

01:20:06.200 --> 01:20:07.100
I got to think of something.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:31.700
Save me from this mad MBA.

01:20:33.530 --> 01:20:35.820
Don't worry. I'll take care of him.

01:20:35.960 --> 01:20:36.580
My hero.

01:20:41.740 --> 01:20:44.720
Flintstone, kiss your bird goodbye.

01:20:47.880 --> 01:20:48.260
Mama.

01:20:49.300 --> 01:20:57.370
Will there be anything else, Mr. Flintstone?

01:20:57.970 --> 01:20:59.670
No, Flintstone. Take the rest of the day off.

01:21:45.360 --> 01:21:46.820
It's time for you and me to interface.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:35.930
True, but I've graciously decided to give you all the credit since it's your name on all the requisition forms.

01:22:40.480 --> 01:22:43.300
Mr. Flintstone, I may not be in on Monday.

01:22:44.040 --> 01:22:47.490
Don't worry, Miss Stone. I'll tell them what you did. I'm sure they'll let you off easy.

01:22:47.650 --> 01:22:55.540
Well, I've been a very bad girl. I have to admit, I was very, very good at it.

01:23:00.250 --> 01:23:02.340
Come on, do it for mommy. Who am I?

01:23:08.650 --> 01:23:09.950
Goodness, you're all right.

01:23:10.500 --> 01:23:14.240
Well, I'm not going to jail, but it won't be easy getting a new job.

01:23:14.970 --> 01:23:17.970
What kind of reference is Mr. Slate going to give me after I destroyed his quarry?

01:23:18.260 --> 01:23:21.460
Oh, none of this was your fault, Fred. I'm sure Mr. Slate will understand.

01:23:22.680 --> 01:23:23.040
Flintstone!

01:23:25.110 --> 01:23:26.410
Sure, now he gets my name right.

01:23:27.340 --> 01:23:28.900
How did this happen?

01:23:30.220 --> 01:23:34.020
Well, Mr. Slate, it all started when the Rebels here wanted to adopt a baby.

01:23:34.560 --> 01:23:38.820
Not that. How did this happen to Cliff?

01:23:39.200 --> 01:23:45.360
Well, you see, Mr. Slate, the machinery went haywire, and the rocks got all crushed up,

01:23:45.400 --> 01:23:47.640
and that got mixed in with water, and that came all down the hill.

01:23:47.860 --> 01:23:49.080
Mr. Slate, I'm sorry.

01:23:49.680 --> 01:23:52.800
Sorry? I love this stuff.

01:23:53.730 --> 01:23:56.130
I'm gonna name it after my daughter, Con Cretia.

01:23:57.540 --> 01:23:59.870
Flintstone, you're a genius.

01:24:01.500 --> 01:24:04.060
Me? Really? Why?

01:24:04.540 --> 01:24:09.540
Don't you see? Thanks to concrete, man can now shape his own destiny.

01:24:09.860 --> 01:24:11.160
The Stone Age is over.

01:24:11.820 --> 01:24:14.660
First thing, I want you to hire back all the men, Flintstone.

01:24:14.980 --> 01:24:17.150
We're going into production immediately.

01:24:17.720 --> 01:24:17.920
We?

01:24:18.340 --> 01:24:22.960
That's right. You are hereby promoted to president of the entire concrete division.

01:24:23.280 --> 01:24:24.400
Yeah, but...

01:24:31.210 --> 01:24:34.590
That's a real nice offer, Mr. Slate, but unfortunately, I'm gonna have to turn you down.

01:24:35.630 --> 01:24:37.010
Don't listen to him, Mr. Slate.

01:24:37.250 --> 01:24:40.230
Fred, it's a great job, and this time you deserve it.

01:24:40.350 --> 01:24:46.040
Barney, all my life I wanted to be a somebody, and when I finally did, I turned into somebody I didn't like.

01:24:46.980 --> 01:24:49.240
Good grief, man. Have you lost your mind?

01:24:49.380 --> 01:24:52.340
This could make you rich, rich beyond your wildest dreams.

01:24:52.740 --> 01:24:56.770
I was always the richest man in the world, just never knew it.

01:24:58.440 --> 01:24:59.980
So if it's okay with you, Mr. Slate...

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:03.110
All I want is my old job back and my old life.

01:25:03.870 --> 01:25:04.270
Fred.

01:25:07.240 --> 01:25:09.760
And two weeks paid vacation for all the men in the quarry,

01:25:09.880 --> 01:25:11.580
an annual cost-of-living increase,

01:25:11.800 --> 01:25:14.500
and those little packets of ketchup in the lunchroom.

01:25:15.150 --> 01:25:15.430
Done.

01:25:16.810 --> 01:25:18.210
Thanks, boss. See you at the company picnic.

01:25:20.720 --> 01:25:23.600
There goes the best executive I ever had.

01:25:24.810 --> 01:25:26.770
Fred, I'm so proud of you.

01:25:26.870 --> 01:25:28.150
And I'm proud of you, Barney.

01:25:28.310 --> 01:25:29.630
And I'm starving. Me too.

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:34.350
say we get some breakfast snake and eggs for everybody my treat great

01:25:34.350 --> 01:25:40.260
honey yes could you spot me a couple bucks i'm a little short

01:26:30.440 --> 01:26:31.420
Get it all time

01:29:13.052 --> 01:29:15.312
Why did I spot a little village by the water?

01:29:15.492 --> 01:29:16.392
Sunset bedrock.

01:29:16.572 --> 01:29:17.912
I met this kid named Freddy.

01:29:18.052 --> 01:29:19.012
Didn't wear no socks.

01:29:19.172 --> 01:29:21.832
He had a part-time gig at the gravel pit slinging rock.

01:29:21.932 --> 01:29:22.912
Said he was into hip-hop.

01:29:23.132 --> 01:29:23.772
Couldn't get the style.

01:29:23.832 --> 01:29:24.892
I told him, go for it.

01:29:25.112 --> 01:29:26.412
Buster first said, what you think?

01:29:26.452 --> 01:29:27.832
I said, your style is prehistoric.

01:29:27.952 --> 01:29:29.192
Sound stuck in the stone age.

01:29:29.252 --> 01:29:29.992
You're still using a...

01:29:42.348 --> 01:29:45.848
Kate Butler saying, tell us how you flip the script and rip pockets.

01:29:46.380 --> 01:29:48.520
One time they said, yeah, yeah, I'm hip, I'm hip.

01:29:48.680 --> 01:29:50.760
Didn't know the time, didn't know about flops.

01:29:50.780 --> 01:29:53.840
So I, you know, I had to show a caveman how to flops.

